# Cloudflare Pages routing. Real files are served first — the per-route HTML
# (/, /add, /settings, /auth/callback, …), /manifest.webmanifest, the PWA icons,
# and the /_expo/* asset bundles — so this rule only catches paths with no
# matching file: chiefly the dynamic /bookmark/<id> route and any deep link.
# Those fall back to the app shell (200, URL preserved), which expo-router then
# client-renders to the correct screen. Capture links like /add?url=… still hit
# the real add.html, so web capture is unaffected.
/*    /index.html    200
